 R←Test_API_131(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;fn1;fn2
⍝ Runs "CompareCommits" on a dot: the working area against the last commit.
⍝ This needs a modified file in the working area, so it acts on the fixture: manufacturing one
⍝ in the project one is actually working on (as this test used to do) means writing a file into
⍝ APLGit2's own APLSource, and leaving it behind whenever the tidy-up does not get a chance.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed
 fn1←fn2←''

 (⊂' r←Counter' ' r←4711')⎕NPUT(∆Folder4,'/APLSource/Counter.aplf')1

 (fn1 fn2)←2↑∆Folder4 G.CompareCommits'.'
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∧/⎕NEXISTS fn1 fn2

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 {}∆Folder4 G.U.RunGitCommand'checkout -- APLSource/Counter.aplf'   ⍝ Leave the fixture as we found it
 :Trap 0 ⋄ FilesAndDirs.DeleteFile fn1 ⋄ :EndTrap
 :Trap 0 ⋄ FilesAndDirs.DeleteFile fn2 ⋄ :EndTrap
⍝Done
